## Claim
Text: "A message will be sent to your phone claiming to show that the Covid19 curve is flattening in India, But It will contain a malicious file"
Claim date: October 15, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Did Indian authorities or cybersecurity agencies issue a warning about a malicious message claiming to show that the COVID-19 curve is flattening in India?
Answer: Based on the search result, the answer is NO. The search result indicates that messages claiming a video about the COVID-19 curve flattening would hack phones were identified as **hoaxes** by fact-checkers and cybersecurity experts, not official warnings by Indian authorities. While India's Computer Emergency Response Team (CERT-IN) did issue a notice, it was specifically about a WhatsApp vulnerability related to a specially crafted MP4 file bug (fixed in November 2019), warning users to update their apps—not about the COVID-19 curve flattening message. As cybersecurity expert Prateek Waghre stated, such an attack was "unlikely," and Sai Krishna Kothapalli of Hackrew confirmed the WhatsApp vulnerability had already been patched. The COVID-19 curve flattening message itself was characterized as a hoax with no credible evidence backing it.

Source URL: https://www.thequint.com/news/webqoof/india-is-doing-it-video-will-hack-your-phone-hoax-message

### Was there a documented case of a malware-laden message circulating in India around October 2020 that used the COVID-19 curve-flattening claim as a lure?
Answer: No — while the exact warning message did circulate widely in India around October 2020 (claiming a WhatsApp video called "India is doing it" showing the COVID-19 curve flattening would hack phones), fact-checkers at BOOM Live debunked it as a hoax, not a documented malware attack. As the article states, "BOOM found that the viral forward is a hoax," and notes that "The message would not have to depend on WhatsApp users to forward it if such a video would have been doing the rounds." BOOM also noted this was the same hoax previously debunked in July 2020 with "Argentina" swapped in for "India."

Source URL: https://www.boomlive.in/fast-check/hoax-message-claims-india-is-doing-it-video-will-hack-your-phone-10210

